,-1,1,"I don't see where this happens in this class but rather than rely on this disable it explicitly at the start of this test. In fact, maybe remove it from the harness and set the value explicitly for…"],["a67e5983_53b8f770",70,-1,0,"not for this CL but just a note: we should clean this up / make it fail more gracefully (with a descriptive error code)."],["d9d0f9ae_284be552",68,-1,1,"would it be useful to have an option to fail-closed if the status is unknown?"],["da5a1224_8be20df7",68,-1,1,"Lets add an #if ENABLE_GLIC here and return true #else the rest. Then you can put the helpers in an #if ENABLE_GLIC"],["e7344d51_5e742604",68,-1,1,"This file/class does lots of things - this name is ambiguous. How about `IsAccountEligibleForActuation`?"],["eccac3d9_9e5a8956",81,-1,1,"Why's this needed? It looks like the inner tests are only looking at the pref in which case this is unneeded. If they're were actually checking whether the toggle correctly affects the policy checker…"],["f3cebd7f_830d5594",68,-1,1,"Maybe call this `ComputeActOnWebCapability` to reflect that it's considering multiple sources..."],["f4300cc8_86df48f4",70,-1,1,"A comment here might be helpful that this is a non-enterprise account in an enterprise managed browser and an account must be signed in for actuation."],["fb6cc460_5b3fa111",68,-1,1,"How about we move the check for `!is_managed` into HasActuationCapability and then this function can be renamed ActuationEnabledForManagedUser"]],0,321],[7151480,20405,14,0.608,0.526,[[0,0.5,10,7],[14,0.278,28,4],[19,0.222,19,3]],[["365df783_ddd8632d",78,0,0,"WDYT of just making this a standalone Feature? silly but I can never remember the format for specifying params on the command line..."]],0,322],[7152303,20405,2,0.143,0.09,[[4,38]],[],0,323],[7150264,20405,13,0.421,0.3,[[14,29]],[["25229831_a3137944",68,0,0,"Isn't this IFTTT backwards? I.e. this is guarding that changes _here_ require changes in glic_user_status_fetcher.cc? Does it work both ways (I expect we want the reverse?)"],["4b982128_7c23bf46",68,0,0,"Do we need to check for non-signed-in explicitly somewhere? Or do we just rely on Glic entrypoints to not be shown?"],["97077a2d_8b656610",68,0,1,"You'll need to add `NO_IFTTT=Introducing IFTTT` to your commit message to silence this."],["bbad5554_81f67406",68,0,1,"This only fetches when `is_managed` GlicUserStatusFetcher::UpdateUserStatus is true. Could you please refer to the code in GUSF and add IFTTT checks for this? (I'm similarly updating a comment and…"],["ce97f015_ae4700b3",68,0,1,"We have tests that check non-managed users, how come they didn't catch this?"]],0,324],[7169207,20411,16,0.737,0.556,[[14,30]],[["4a3dc273_06fd4e4f",1,0,1,"I guess this is now unused? It's helpful to have even a one-sentence description of why this is a cleanup (e.g. dead code after crrev.com/####)"]],0,325],[7200745,20418,39,1.341,1.058,[[14,31]],[],0,326],[7208442,20423,33,1.341,1.058,[[20,22]],[["2fb78e15_178106b8",82,0,1,"I think I'm missing something about this line -- don't these run synchronously, as if you just wrote `OnGlicButtonAnimationEnded(); ShowGlicActorNudge(nudge_text)`?"],["e0e06243_2b7db967",1,0,0,"It might be worthwhile to create an animation controller to help manage the different animations that run on the button. This way you can query the controller to know if certain animations are…"]],0,327],[7214167,20424,10,0.384,0.302,[[24,21]],[["b49573eb_f7f9d4d7",83,-1,1,"I'd just bump it by a year, think we'll need to monitor this for a while."]],0,328],[7227878,20427,155,4.21,3.407,[[14,0.411,32,63],[0,0.211,11,36],[9,0.126,3,19],[16,0.069,2,10],[26,0.063,0,9],[24,0.063,22,10],[27,0.057,0,8]],[["5c0623cb_a2e1d67d",84,0,0,"This is repeated?"],["895d2ab8_35004bec",46,0,1,"I am not sure if this enum is logged in the metrics. If so, it's missing a comment and all other values should be also numbered."],["a63d345c_72f36298",85,0,1,"nit: don't comment this out, just change the label to \"(Obsolete) Error. Removed in 